{
  "requirement": "The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet file = std::path::PathBuf::from(\"src/auth.rs\");\n```\n\nAn item within that file uses the path and selector in `OutlineId` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.source_addresses`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values. This covers addresses the tools return and addresses they accept.\n2. An item inside a file is addressed by the path and selector in `OutlineId`. The identity rules themselves belong to the cited `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, so I did not reassess them.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **Listing returns relative `PathBuf` values.**\n  - `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` collects the listing and asserts exact relative strings such as `keep.txt`, `src/nested.txt` and `.visible`. It also asserts that ignored and excluded paths are absent.\n  - `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` asserts `listed[0] == Path::new(\"src/one.txt\")`.\n- **Accepted addresses are project-relative.**\n  - `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` reads a relative path successfully.\n  - The same test rejects `../outside.txt`, an absolute path and a missing path.\n  - `src/sources/tests.rs#fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` rejects outside-root and symlink escapes.\n- **Items carry path and selector.**\n  - `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` asserts `parsed.id().path == Path::new(\"note.txt\")` and `selector == \"\"`.\n  - `tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]` asserts that structural matches carry `node.path == Path::new(\"visible.rs\")`.\n  - `tests/search.rs#fn[outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths]` builds `OutlineId::new(PathBuf, selector)`. It asserts that `path` and `selector` are kept unchanged, including for an opaque path, the empty root selector and a percent-encoded selector. It also asserts that malformed selectors are rejected.\n- **Additional test.** `src/sources/tests.rs#fn[addresses_preserve_opaque_fields_and_compare_each_identity_component]` exercises the internal `ResourceId`-based `OutlineId`. That is not the `PathBuf` form the requirement describes. It does no harm, but I did not count it as coverage of the subject.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found none. Each obligation has a test with real assertions on the returned or accepted address values. Behavior that returns absolute paths, returns non-relative paths, or drops the selector would fail these assertions. Identity and equality semantics are covered by the cited `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, not here.",
  "references": "df11f66fd68a124ab40cef9071bf3bccaac4decfa892b3cefd1b981b483de25d",
  "inputs": [
